{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b0ce3cfc","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"384a87f9-1bbf-478e-ae18-66e810243be8","_uuid":"220c719e-c337-4fcc-af50-c6c43039f231","collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":0.005092,"end_time":"2026-10-02T02:35:21.277739+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-02T02:35:21.272647+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# Stage 4: Alternating Jointly-Optimised BGNN Pipeline\n","## Audit-Hardened Edition (v2) — Protocol-Aligned with Stages 1, 2, and 3\n","\n","### Core Responsibilities\n","1. **Full-Pipeline Integration**: Jointly couple tabular decision structures with relational graph message passing via alternating functional-gradient optimization.\n","2. **Strict Time Causality**: Ensure all feature scalers, PCA projections, graph predecessors, and boosting updates depend strictly on historical data ($t_{\\text{hist}} < t_{\\text{curr}}$).\n","3. **Two-Pass Protocol Separation**:\n","   - **Pass A (Evaluation)**: 1-day boundary embargo on validation blocks to compute honest, unbiased benchmark metrics.\n","   - **Pass B (Scoring)**: Embargo lifted to generate 100% coverage on Blocks 2–4, 75% coverage on Block 1 via expanding sub-folds, and full holdout inference on Block 5 via a frozen model.\n","4. **Monotonic Blending Gate**: Enforce exact tabular fallback ($\beta_i = 0$) for isolated cold-start nodes while dynamically weighting connected components.\n","5. **Statistical Rigour**: Isotonic probability calibration on inner stopping splits and Benjamini–Hochberg FDR control on confirmatory bootstrap tests.\n","\n","### Refinement patch notes — six implemented groups\n","1. Pooled bootstrap uses the exact embargoed fold-mask union with identical subset/finite-pair filtering and disjoint aligned-row count assertions, even when individual tests are skipped.\n","2. Stage 1/optional Stage 3 loading validates IDs, many-to-one alignment, numeric probabilities and strict metadata. Filled fallbacks require explicit availability plus recognised original scoring provenance; unavailable rows remain NaN.\n","3. A pre-feature Stage 1 coverage gate exempts only the first chronological B1 seed slice, reports per-block required/exempt/invalid counts and rejects all other original-score gaps.\n","4. Fold, B1 sub-fold and frozen-OOT card/device extraction and causality audits share the configured lookback and retain deterministic audit records.\n","5. The boosting arm advances only for exactly one material, FDR-significant pooled confirmatory H3a result; all other cases fail closed.\n","6. OOF IDs, probabilities, flags, exact fills and slice provenance are validated **before CSV export**; disabled calibration exports NaN. The manifest records the gate, coverage, audits, export checks and streaming SHA-256 fingerprints of actually consumed raw/optional identity/decision ledger/OOF/reference-result files. Unavailable optional inputs retain null paths/hashes; unused Stage 2 results are not fingerprinted.\n","\n","**Deferred — needs approval:** missing-device sentinel graph/schema changes and minimum edge-share/beta audit. Entity UID construction, sentinel edges and beta behaviour are unchanged; no deferred-item graph audit is implemented.\n","\n","**Execution/provenance scope:** no training rerun, real-data validation, new metrics or upstream retrieval was performed (real inputs were not attached). Prior policy, architecture, parameters, training/calibration/scoring and time split otherwise remain unchanged. Old outputs, execution counts and run metadata are cleared. Use **Fresh Kernel / Run All** with the real inputs. The embedded deterministic code hash covers the ordered published code-source bundle, excluding its own explicitly marked declaration; it was verified against the final sources and must be regenerated after code edits. Notebook execution without `__file__` records a truthful null script-file hash, not an invented notebook-file hash. Input fingerprints